  <section id="story" class="c"><div class="sec rv"><div><h2>Key decisions.</h2></div><div class="t"><div class="item"><h3>Platform</h3><p>The team evaluated five platforms (Glide, Lovable, Replit, Claude Code and Codex) and selected Replit, the only one with an officially guided route to <span class="nw">App Store</span> publishing.</p></div><div class="item"><h3>Requirements</h3><p>Requirements were defined from scratch together with the sponsor and organised into 10 modules, delivered over four sprints.</p></div><div class="item"><h3>Quality gate</h3><p>An independent tester signed off every feature before it was considered complete. The pre-release check ran 49 API tests and 65 app tests, and all passed.</p></div><div class="item"><h3>Privacy</h3><p>Contact details are hidden by default and become visible only after a meeting is accepted, a rule enforced on the server. Reporting, blocking and in-app account deletion are built in.</p></div></div></div></section>
